@startuml direct-rialto-drm-session-state
title RialtoMediaKeySessionAdapter KeyState lifecycle (as driven by AAMP's DrmSessionManager)

[*] --> KEY_INIT : adapter created by\nmakeRialtoSessionCreator()

KEY_INIT --> KEY_ERROR : generateDRMSession()\n[no valid RialtoMediaKeySystem]
KEY_INIT --> KEY_ERROR_SESSION_CREATE_FAILED : generateDRMSession()\n[createKeySession or\ngenerateRequest failed]
KEY_INIT --> KEY_INIT : generateDRMSession() OK\n(Rialto session exists, mksId valid)

KEY_INIT --> KEY_ERROR : generateKeyRequest()\nsets KEY_ERROR first;\nstays there on challenge timeout\nor empty challenge
KEY_ERROR --> KEY_PENDING : challenge received\n(onChallenge, not individualisation)

KEY_PENDING --> KEY_READY : processDRMKey()\n[update OK, any key USABLE]
KEY_PENDING --> KEY_ERROR : processDRMKey()\n[update failed, key-status timeout,\nOUTPUT_RESTRICTED (HDCP error)\nor no usable key]

KEY_READY --> KEY_ERROR : renewal: onLicenseRenewal ->\nlicenseRenewalThread -> generateKeyRequest()\n(then KEY_PENDING -> KEY_READY as above)

KEY_READY --> KEY_INIT : clearDecryptContext()\n[close + releaseKeySession,\nderegister, mksId = -1]
KEY_ERROR --> KEY_INIT : clearDecryptContext()
KEY_ERROR_SESSION_CREATE_FAILED --> KEY_INIT : clearDecryptContext()

KEY_INIT --> [*] : ~adapter (DrmSessionManager\ndeletes the slot's session)

note right of KEY_READY
  Key status changes after KEY_READY
  (for example EXPIRED) are cached in
  RialtoMediaKeySession but nothing acts
  on them; failures surface later as
  PlaybackError::DECRYPTION.
end note
@enduml
